// PIN (kebab-stdlib-restructure): `_` is no longer a legal name-char — `foo_bar`
// must be REJECTED with a demangle-aware hint (use `foo-bar`; `_` is reserved
// for digit separators, G4). RED today — the lexer still ACCEPTS `_` in
// identifiers (lexer.zig:68,72), so no error is produced and this
// EXPECT=FRONTEND_COMPILE_ERROR test fails. Tighten to expected_patterns.txt
// once the G4 message text lands.
import std/io

~event foo_bar {}

~std.io:println(text: "underscore should have been rejected")
